error[lower::type-check::type-mismatch]: Type mismatch
   ╭▸ 
 8 │       ["input", "x", "String"],
   │                       ────── this is of type `!`
   ‡
11 │     "inputs": { "#struct": { "x": { "#literal": 1 } } }
   │                                                 ━ `Integer` cannot be a subtype of `!`
   │
   ├ help: Only the `!` (Never) type itself can be a subtype of `!`. Any type with values cannot be a subtype of `!`, which by definition has no values.
   ╰ note: In type theory, the `!` type (also called 'bottom type' or 'Never') is a type with no values. It can be a subtype of any type, but only `!` can be a subtype of `!`.